INT. AUCTION HOUSE, FREIGHT ELEVATOR - NIGHT

A cage of scuffed steel, floor stenciled with weight limits. The elevator hums, descending through darkness. A crate the size of a coffin stands on a hand truck.

LORENZO "ENZO" MARCHETTI, 50s, tuxedo, bow tie crooked, holds the truck handles. NOOR HASHEMI, 30s, in a janitor's jumpsuit, mop bucket by her ankle. OSCAR "OZZIE" LIN, 20s, headphones around his neck, crouches by a panel with a screwdriver. At the back, DARCY LUND, 60s, an auction-house guard in uniform, hums a tune. He has not noticed anything.

ENZO
(whispering)
Floor three.

NOOR
Keep humming, Darcy.

DARCY
(cheerfully)
Always do.

The elevator shudders. Noor grips the rail.

NOOR
Ozzie, the camera.

OZZIE
Looped. Eight seconds.

ENZO
Eight seconds is nothing.

OZZIE
It's what the tape gives.

NOOR
(over Ozzie)
Where's the other guard?

DARCY
(over Noor)
Which one?

ENZO
Darcy, the other guard.

DARCY
Oh. Lunchtime.

Everyone exhales. The elevator stops. The cage door slides open on a dim lobby with a marble floor and a vault door ten feet tall.

ENZO
(quietly)
Showtime.

They roll the crate out. The wheels squeak. Darcy hums louder.

BASE (V.O.)
(a voice from Darcy's radio)
Base to Darcy. Base to Darcy. Status.

Darcy lifts the radio.

DARCY
Base, Darcy. All clear. Just a delivery.

BASE (V.O.)
Delivery? At this hour?

DARCY
Antique. Very heavy.

BASE (V.O.)
Copy. Stay put.

Silence. Enzo's eyes narrow at Darcy. Noor slides a hand to her pocket.

OZZIE
Eight seconds. Seven. Six.

DARCY
(into the radio, smiling)
Base, actually, there's a problem.

Everyone freezes.

BASE (V.O.)
What problem?

DARCY
My feet hurt.

A long beat. Then the radio laughs.

BASE (V.O.)
Roger that. Sit down, Darcy.

Darcy sits on the crate and unlaces a shoe. Enzo and Noor stare. Ozzie laughs once, high, into his hand.

NOOR
(whispering)
He's good.

ENZO
(whispering)
He's the best liar I ever hired.

OZZIE
Three. Two.

The vault door swings open on its own, lit from within by a pale green glow. Enzo steps toward it.

ENZO
(under his breath)
Hello, beautiful.

DARCY
Mind the wheels, boss.

BASE (V.O.)
Darcy, say again. Who are you talking to?

Darcy looks at the radio. Then at the three of them. He sets it on the crate, very gently, and switches it off.

DARCY
Nobody.
